Select Tilck's ACPICA environment header instead of Linux's.

ACPICA picks a platform header by compiler predefine, and Tilck is not
in its table: without this it takes the __linux__ branch and pulls in
aclinux.h, which assumes a Linux kernel's headers and locking
primitives. Point that branch at Tilck's own actilck.h.

The "// patched" markers are kept from the in-place edit this replaces,
so the rebuilt source is identical to what the gsubs produced.

--- a/source/include/platform/acenv.h
+++ b/source/include/platform/acenv.h
@@ -305,8 +305,8 @@
 
 #endif
 
-#if defined(_LINUX) || defined(__linux__)
-#include "aclinux.h"
+#if defined(__TILCK_KERNEL__)   // patched
+#include "tilck/acpi/actilck.h" // patched
 
 #elif defined(_APPLE) || defined(__APPLE__)
 #include "acmacosx.h"
